`snapshot diff` is the offline half of the `.zsnap` verb (#219, RFC 13 §4.4):
two files in, no session, and the one contract the section makes
non-negotiable — **both spans stated**, in the envelope and in the caveat —
visible on every exit code. The two fixtures are the shared report fixtures
written through the engine's own writer (`tests/render.rs` keeps them in
step), so this case and the render snapshots read the same bytes.

**1 — they differ.** A difference *is* the finding. Every row is tagged by
kind (`added`, `removed`, `changed`), and a `changed` row carries only the
facets that moved: the disk value carries a `value` diff, the second host's
health carries a `value` diff *and* a `holder` pair.

```console
$ zenctl snapshot diff tests/cmd/fixtures/a.zsnap tests/cmd/fixtures/b.zsnap
? 1
{"a":{"answered":6,"asked":1,"base":"acme","collected_at":"2026-09-06T00:00:00Z","collection_span_s":1.25,"roster":2,"selectors":["acme/v1/**"],"superseded":1,"zsnap":1},"b":{"answered":5,"asked":1,"base":"acme","collected_at":"2026-09-06T00:05:00Z","collection_span_s":0.8,"roster":2,"selectors":["acme/v1/**"],"zsnap":1},"notes":[{"cite":"RFC 13 §4.4","text":"a: span 1.25s at 2026-09-06T00:00:00Z, b: span 0.80s at 2026-09-06T00:05:00Z — each side was collected over its span, not at an instant"},{"cite":"RFC 09 §5.1 O4","text":"keys compared verbatim — no origin alignment was asked, so the same host under a different origin reads as removed and added"}],"report":"snapshot-diff","unchanged":2}
{"key":"acme/v1/h-9b2e4c7a1d05/telemetry/sysinfo/disk/var-log/used","row":"added"}
{"key":"acme/v1/h-9b2e4c7a1d05/state/logs/rotated","row":"removed"}
{"key":"acme/v1/h-3fa9c2d41b7e/telemetry/sysinfo/disk/var-log/used","row":"changed","timestamp":["7f3b2a1c00000001/ab12","7f3b2a1c00000002/ab12"],"value":{"changes":[{"new":42.0,"old":41.0,"op":"changed","path":"value"}],"truncated":0}}
{"holder":[{"kind":"storage_only","origin":"h-9b2e4c7a1d05"},{"answered_by":"unknown","kind":"live","origin":"h-9b2e4c7a1d05"}],"key":"acme/v1/h-9b2e4c7a1d05/state/sysinfo/health","row":"changed","timestamp":["7f3b2a1c00000001/ab12","7f3b2a1c00000002/cd34"],"value":{"changes":[{"new":"ok","old":"degraded","op":"changed","path":"status"}],"truncated":0}}
a: span 1.25s at 2026-09-06T00:00:00Z, b: span 0.80s at 2026-09-06T00:05:00Z — each side was collected over its span, not at an instant (RFC 13 §4.4)
keys compared verbatim — no origin alignment was asked, so the same host under a different origin reads as removed and added (RFC 09 §5.1 O4)

```

**0 — identical on every facet.** The clean answer, with the spans still
stated: an empty diff is a statement about two collections, not about an
instant.

```console
$ zenctl snapshot diff tests/cmd/fixtures/a.zsnap tests/cmd/fixtures/a.zsnap
{"a":{"answered":6,"asked":1,"base":"acme","collected_at":"2026-09-06T00:00:00Z","collection_span_s":1.25,"roster":2,"selectors":["acme/v1/**"],"superseded":1,"zsnap":1},"b":{"answered":6,"asked":1,"base":"acme","collected_at":"2026-09-06T00:00:00Z","collection_span_s":1.25,"roster":2,"selectors":["acme/v1/**"],"superseded":1,"zsnap":1},"notes":[{"cite":"RFC 13 §4.4","text":"a: span 1.25s at 2026-09-06T00:00:00Z, b: span 1.25s at 2026-09-06T00:00:00Z — each side was collected over its span, not at an instant"},{"cite":"RFC 09 §5.1 O4","text":"keys compared verbatim — no origin alignment was asked, so the same host under a different origin reads as removed and added"}],"report":"snapshot-diff","unchanged":5}
a: span 1.25s at 2026-09-06T00:00:00Z, b: span 1.25s at 2026-09-06T00:00:00Z — each side was collected over its span, not at an instant (RFC 13 §4.4)
keys compared verbatim — no origin alignment was asked, so the same host under a different origin reads as removed and added (RFC 09 §5.1 O4)

```

**2 — the question could not be asked.** A file that will not read is the
reserved non-verdict, never a 1 claiming the two differ — the same split
`check schema` guards.

```console
$ zenctl snapshot diff tests/cmd/fixtures/a.zsnap tests/cmd/fixtures/missing.zsnap
? 2
Error: open tests/cmd/fixtures/missing.zsnap

Caused by:
    No such file or directory (os error 2)
snapshot diff: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

```

The origin-alignment flags parse today so the shape is stable, and refuse
until chunk DD lands the alignment — a diff that silently ignored `--map`
would compare the wrong keys.

```console
$ zenctl snapshot diff --normalize-origins tests/cmd/fixtures/a.zsnap tests/cmd/fixtures/b.zsnap
? 2
Error: --normalize-origins / --map: origin alignment is not implemented in this build (chunk DD)

```
